	(text "BASEBAND NOTES (one file, two instances: Baseband_I 8xx, Baseband_Q 9xx; every signal-path part has Matched = I/Q)\n- In-amp INA819 (DigiKey sub for INA826, same pinout): G = 1 + 50k / RG = 1 + 50 / 5.49 = 10.11.\n  5 V single supply, VCM = VREF = 2.5 V: centred in DS Fig. 7-52 (VS = 5 V, VREF 2.5 V curve), ~1 V margin both ways.\n- HPF unity Sallen-Key: C1 = C2 = 100n C0G 1206, R1 113k (to OUT), R2 226k (to VREF_BUF): f0 = 9.96 Hz, Q = 0.707.\n- Gain x4: 1 + 10.0k / 3.32k = 4.01. DNP alternates 10.0k (x2) / 1.10k (x10) in parallel with Rg.\n- LPF unity Sallen-Key: R1 = R2 = 11.3k, C1 6.8n (to OUT), C2 3.3n (to GND): f0 = 2.97 kHz, Q = 0.72.\n- Coupling caps C1/C2/C12: 470n C0G 1206 (1 uF C0G is 1825/2220 only). Input with 100k bias: fc = 3.4 Hz;\n  output into PCM1808 60k: fc = 5.6 Hz. Both well under the 10 Hz HPF (adds ~1.7 dB at 10 Hz, ~0.5 dB at 20 Hz).\n- VREF: 10.0k / 10.0k 0.1% from +5V_A = 2.500 V (mid-rail), 47u polymer, follower + 47R -> VREF_BUF + 100n C0G.\n  Bias, HPF R2, Rg and INA REF return to VREF_BUF only. No X5R/X7R on signal nets, VREF or VREF_BUF.\n- Op-amp OPA4388 (DigiKey sub for OPA4376, same pinout): zero-drift, no 1/f noise."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
